From 1d39fbe53ea7def77f130e84d89bb0c83e8983f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 07:02:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] avcodec/ppc: add AltiVec VP9 16x16/32x32 inverse
 transforms (O2)

Full TX_16X16 (idct16/iadst16, all four txtype combos) and TX_32X32
(idct32) AltiVec paths, replacing the previous eob==1-only DC wrappers
that fell back to C for everything else; the DC fast paths are kept.

Design: bit-for-bit the C reference (idct16_1d / iadst16_1d /
idct32_1d under itxfm_wrapper), 8-bit only.  A 1D pass runs on 8 of
the N columns at a time on the 8x8 section's s32x8 multiply helpers,
but unlike the 8x8 code every value is narrowed back to int16 right
after its (+(1<<13))>>14 rounding and the butterflies run as plain
wrapping int16 adds - the layout the aarch64 NEON version keeps in
.8h registers, legal because the C reference stores every such value
in int16 tmp[]/out[] or feeds it to a later int16-operand multiply.
iadst16's first/third multiply blocks stay unrounded s32 exactly like
the C's t0..t15 (sums < 2^31 for all coefficient pairs).  The two-pass
wrapper keeps pass-a output in a transposed vec_s16 scratch (vector k
of column group g = tmp_C[8g..8g+7][k]) and gathers pass-b inputs with
8x8 transposes; outputs go through an 8-wide bits==6 add/store
(store8_row, no RMW).

Registered unconditionally (no per-CPU gate - no bench data yet).

Validated: qemu -cpu 7400 checkasm vp9dsp bit-exact vs C on seeds
1/42/777/12345/31337; full suite 590/590 (+3: the 16x16 adst combos;
the dct_dct 16x16/32x32 names existed already via the DC wrappers);
per-name --bench listing shows _altivec entries for all sub-eob
levels; -D_ARCH_PWR4 (G5-shape) compile warning-free.  Real-G4/G5
bench pending (qemu TCG ratios are not predictive).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HcoCJhZQdwZvDdC836fitg
